; /XTRA
;; blit-last-write.ab3 -- does a blit's last word go astray when the next blit's destination is written too soon?
;; Compile in UAE. Not part of the game. For the stray one-pixel rows (the main project's candidates notes): the stamp check of 2026-11-06 found
;; each stray to be a word MOVED: the last word of a tile's plane 2 blit missing, and the same word in plane 3 of the same
;; bitmap exactly $20000 bytes higher. That is a blit's last D write landing between the two halves of the next blit's long
;; write to BLTDPT (the 68020 writes the high word first): the new high word with the old low word.
;;
;; Two bitmaps the size of the game's world bitmaps (3904 x 256, 4 planes) are cleared, and a solid 16x16 tile (pen 15: every
;; word $FFFF in every plane) is blitted into every other cell, a checkerboard, cell after cell as the stamp does. Then every
;; word is read: a blitted cell's word that is not $FFFF is MISSING, an empty cell's word that is not 0 is a STRAY. Four ways
;; of blitting, #ROUNDS rounds of #PASSES_A_ROUND passes each (below):
;;   method 0  Blitz's Block (the game's stamp)
;;   method 1  a blit of our own, one plane at a time: wait as the libraries do, then BLTDPT first, then the rest
;;   method 2  as 1, but after the wait a second read of DMACONR and a second wait
;;   method 3  as 1, but BLTDPT written last, just before BLTSIZE (five register writes after the wait)
;; Expected if the idea is right: methods 0 and 1 leave some (rarely), method 3 none. Each method's time (CIA-A frames,
;; the scans included) is kept too. It runs in Blitz mode for a minute or so (the screen does not change), then writes
;; results/blit-last-write-results.txt. A stray that lands outside both bitmaps lands in other Chip RAM: if the proof
;; crashes, that is the likely reason, and worth knowing too.
;; The display is the game's (SparkyDave.ab3, as proofs/allstars-scene.ab3 has it): a 16 line HUD list that loads the colours
;; and a 208 line dual playfield world list, 8 planes at fetch mode 1, 8 sprite channels, showing bitmap 0 over a back bitmap
;; the game's size. The first version of this proof had no display of its own, the chip bus nearly idle, and found nothing
;; in 39,040 tiles a method (2026-11-06); the game, with its display on, had 7 words in about 45,000. So this one loads the
;; bus as the game does. (The sprite channels are given no sprite: a band of garbage under the picture is only that.)
;; Rounds (third version, 2026-11-06): the second version caught one moved word in 39,040 tiles (Block, $20000 apart), too few
;; to compare the methods. A round clears both bitmaps once, blits the checkerboard #PASSES_A_ROUND times over without clearing,
;; then scans once: a stray lands in an empty cell and stays, so the strays add up over the round (each is one event; a
;; missing word is written again by the next pass, so the missing count is the last pass's only). The blits' own time is
;; counted apart from the scans', so a method's cost can be compared.
;; Progress: the screen's colour 0 is set while it scans, one colour a method (red, green, blue, yellow), bright and dark on
;; alternate passes, so a hang shows as a colour that stays. The results file is written after each method, so a run cut
;; short by a reset still says how far it got.

WBStartup

#WORLD_A_BM     = 0
#WORLD_B_BM     = 1
#SOURCE_BM      = 2
#TILE_SHAPE     = 0
#WORLD_W        = 3904
#WORLD_H        = 256
#WORLD_WORDS    = 244
#CELL_ROWS      = 16
#ROUNDS         = 5
#PASSES_A_ROUND = 20
#METHODS        = 4
#KEPT_MAX       = 60
#BROKEN_WORDS   = 2000
#HUD_BM         = 3
#BACK_BM        = 4
#HUD_LINE       = 44
#HUD_H          = 16
#LIST_GAP       = 3
#VIEW_H         = 208
#VIEW_TOP       = 32
#BACK_W         = 1088
#BACK_H         = 288
#HUD_W          = 320
#HUD_FLAGS      = $11414
#WORLD_FLAGS    = $11438
#PF2_OFFSET     = $1c00

;; The counts for each method, and the words kept (the first #KEPT_MAX over all methods): the method, the pass, the bitmap,
;; the plane, x, y, the word found, whether it is missing (True) or a stray (False), and its address.
Dim methodMissing.l(#METHODS - 1)
Dim methodStrays.l(#METHODS - 1)
Dim methodFrames.l(#METHODS - 1)
Dim methodBlitFrames.l(#METHODS - 1)
;; Whether a method was stopped as broken (a pass with more than #BROKEN_WORDS words wrong: the blit itself is wrong, not the
;; rare word), its passes run, the methods done so far (the results file is written after each), and the colour shown.
Dim methodBroken.w(#METHODS - 1)
Dim methodPasses.w(#METHODS - 1)
methodsDone.w = 0
progressColour.w = 0
stageTrail$ = ""
Dim methodColour.w(#METHODS - 1)
methodColour(0) = $F00
methodColour(1) = $0F0
methodColour(2) = $00F
methodColour(3) = $FF0
keptCount.w = 0
Dim keptMethod.w(#KEPT_MAX - 1)
Dim keptPass.w(#KEPT_MAX - 1)
Dim keptBitmap.w(#KEPT_MAX - 1)
Dim keptPlane.w(#KEPT_MAX - 1)
Dim keptX.w(#KEPT_MAX - 1)
Dim keptY.w(#KEPT_MAX - 1)
Dim keptFound.w(#KEPT_MAX - 1)
Dim keptMissing.w(#KEPT_MAX - 1)
Dim keptAddress.l(#KEPT_MAX - 1)

;; One 16x16 tile, all planes, from sourceStruct's bitmap (its top left) into destStruct's at byte offset destOffset in each
;; plane, one blit a plane, a straight copy (A to D, minterm $F0). blitMode is the method less one (see the header): 0 BLTDPT
;; first after one wait, 1 the same after a second wait, 2 BLTDPT last. In Blitz mode, which owns the blitter.
;; d0 sourceStruct, d1 destStruct, d2 destOffset, d3 blitMode; a4 to a6 and d7 are Blitz's and are left alone.
Statement AsmBlockTile{sourceStruct.l, destStruct.l, destOffset.l, blitMode.w}
  MOVE.l d0,a0
  MOVE.l d1,a1
  LEA $DFF000,a2
  MOVE.w (a0),d4
  SUBQ.w #2,d4
  MOVE.w (a1),d5
  SUBQ.w #2,d5
  LEA 8(a0),a0
  LEA 8(a1),a1
  MOVEQ #3,d6
abtPlane:
  MOVE.l (a0)+,a3
  MOVE.l (a1)+,d0
  ADD.l d2,d0
  BTST #6,2(a2)
abtWaitFirst:
  BTST #6,2(a2)
  BNE.w abtWaitFirst
  CMP.w #1,d3
  BNE.w abtNoSecondWait
  TST.w 2(a2)
abtWaitSecond:
  BTST #6,2(a2)
  BNE.w abtWaitSecond
abtNoSecondWait:
  CMP.w #2,d3
  BEQ.w abtPointerLast
  MOVE.l d0,84(a2)
  MOVE.l #$09F00000,64(a2)
  MOVE.l #$FFFFFFFF,68(a2)
  MOVE.w d4,100(a2)
  MOVE.w d5,102(a2)
  MOVE.l a3,80(a2)
  BRA.w abtStart
abtPointerLast:
  MOVE.l #$09F00000,64(a2)
  MOVE.l #$FFFFFFFF,68(a2)
  MOVE.w d4,100(a2)
  MOVE.w d5,102(a2)
  MOVE.l a3,80(a2)
  MOVE.l d0,84(a2)
abtStart:
  MOVE.w #$0401,88(a2)
  DBRA d6,abtPlane
  AsmExit
End Statement

; CIA-A's frame counter (the vertical blanks), 24 bits: the high byte read first latches the rest.
Function.l CiaFrames{}
  highByte.l = Peek.b($BFEA01) AND 255
  middleByte.l = Peek.b($BFE901) AND 255
  lowByte.l = Peek.b($BFE801) AND 255
  Function Return highByte*65536 + middleByte*256 + lowByte
End Function

;; Every word of one bitmap against the checkerboard: in cell row r, the cells whose column + r is even are blitted ($FFFF),
;; the others empty (0). Compared a long (two cells) at a time; only a long that differs is looked at word by word.
Statement ScanBitmap{bitmapNumber.w, methodIndex.w, roundIndex.w}
  SHARED methodMissing(), methodStrays(), keptCount, keptMethod(), keptPass(), keptBitmap(), keptPlane(), keptX(), keptY()
  SHARED keptFound(), keptMissing(), keptAddress(), progressColour
  structAddress.l = Addr BitMap(bitmapNumber)
  rowBytes.l = Peek.w(structAddress)
  For planeIndex.w = 0 To 3
    planeBase.l = Peek.l(structAddress + 8 + planeIndex*4)
    For pixelRow.w = 0 To #WORLD_H - 1
      ; The screen's colour 0, every row, so the Copper's own setting of it each frame does not hide the progress.
      Poke.w $DFF180, progressColour
      rowStart.l = planeBase + pixelRow*rowBytes
      cellRow.w = pixelRow/16
      wantedLong.l = $FFFF0000
      If cellRow MOD 2 = 1 Then wantedLong = $0000FFFF
      For pairIndex.w = 0 To #WORLD_WORDS/2 - 1
        If Peek.l(rowStart + pairIndex*4) <> wantedLong
          For wordIndex.w = pairIndex*2 To pairIndex*2 + 1
            wordAddress.l = rowStart + wordIndex*2
            foundWord.w = Peek.w(wordAddress)
            wantedWord.w = 0
            If (wordIndex + cellRow) MOD 2 = 0 Then wantedWord = -1
            If foundWord <> wantedWord
              isMissing.w = False
              If wantedWord = -1
                isMissing = True
                methodMissing(methodIndex) = methodMissing(methodIndex) + 1
              Else
                methodStrays(methodIndex) = methodStrays(methodIndex) + 1
              EndIf
              If keptCount < #KEPT_MAX
                keptMethod(keptCount) = methodIndex
                keptPass(keptCount) = roundIndex
                keptBitmap(keptCount) = bitmapNumber
                keptPlane(keptCount) = planeIndex
                keptX(keptCount) = wordIndex*16
                keptY(keptCount) = pixelRow
                keptFound(keptCount) = foundWord
                keptMissing(keptCount) = isMissing
                keptAddress(keptCount) = wordAddress
                keptCount = keptCount + 1
              EndIf
            EndIf
          Next
        EndIf
      Next
    Next
  Next
End Statement

;; The trail of steps reached, written whole to results/blit-last-write-stages.txt at each step: the last line is the last
;; step reached before a hang. In Amiga mode (WriteStages{}); MarkStage{} is the call from Blitz mode.
Statement WriteStages{}
  SHARED stageTrail$
  If WriteFile(1, "sparky-dave:game/proofs/results/blit-last-write-stages.txt")
    FileOutput 1
    Print stageTrail$
    CloseFile 1
    DefaultOutput
  EndIf
End Statement

Statement MarkStage{stageText$}
  SHARED stageTrail$
  stageTrail$ = stageTrail$ + stageText$ + Chr$(10)
  QAMIGA
  WriteStages{}
  BLITZ
End Statement

;; The checkerboard into one bitmap by one method. markRows True marks each cell row in the stage trail (the first pass of
;; the first bitmap of each method): a hang always at row 0 is a blit that never returns, one at a row that changes from run
;; to run is a stray write that broke the machine.
Statement BlitCheckerboard{bitmapNumber.w, methodIndex.w, markRows.w}
  sourceStruct.l = Addr BitMap(#SOURCE_BM)
  destStruct.l = Addr BitMap(bitmapNumber)
  rowBytes.l = Peek.w(destStruct)
  Use BitMap bitmapNumber
  For cellRow.w = 0 To #CELL_ROWS - 1
    If markRows = True
      MarkStage{"  method " + Str$(methodIndex) + ", cell row " + Str$(cellRow) + " starting"}
      Use BitMap bitmapNumber
    EndIf
    For cellColumn.w = cellRow MOD 2 To #WORLD_WORDS - 1 Step 2
      If methodIndex = 0
        Block #TILE_SHAPE, cellColumn*16, cellRow*16
      Else
        AsmBlockTile{sourceStruct, destStruct, cellRow*16*rowBytes + cellColumn*2, methodIndex - 1}
      EndIf
    Next
  Next
End Statement

;; The results so far (the methods done), in Amiga mode: written after each method, so a run cut short still has them.
Statement WriteResults{}
  SHARED methodMissing(), methodStrays(), methodFrames(), methodBlitFrames(), methodBroken(), methodPasses(), methodsDone, keptCount, keptMethod()
  SHARED keptPass(), keptBitmap(), keptPlane(), keptX(), keptY(), keptFound(), keptMissing(), keptAddress()
  If WriteFile(0, "sparky-dave:game/proofs/results/blit-last-write-results.txt")
    FileOutput 0
    NPrint "blit-last-write: a solid 16x16 tile into every other cell of two 3904 x 256 x 4 bitmaps, under the game's display"
    NPrint #ROUNDS, " rounds a method, each ", #PASSES_A_ROUND, " passes over the same checkerboard, then one scan"
    NPrint "tiles a pass: ", #CELL_ROWS*#WORLD_WORDS, " (4 planes each); missing: a blitted word not $FFFF after a round's last pass;"
    NPrint "stray: an empty word not 0 (they stay, so a round's strays are all its passes')"
    NPrint "bitmap 0 bytes a row ", Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#WORLD_A_BM))
    For planeIndex.w = 0 To 3
      NPrint "  bitmap 0 plane ", planeIndex, " at $", Hex$(Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#WORLD_A_BM) + 8 + planeIndex*4))
    Next
    For planeIndex = 0 To 3
      NPrint "  bitmap 1 plane ", planeIndex, " at $", Hex$(Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#WORLD_B_BM) + 8 + planeIndex*4))
    Next
    NPrint ""
    NPrint "methods started: ", methodsDone, " of ", #METHODS, " (the file is written after each round: the last may be part done)"
    NPrint "method  missing  strays  frames (CIA-A, all)  frames blitting  passes  tiles"
    For methodIndex.w = 0 To methodsDone - 1
      Print methodIndex, "  ", methodMissing(methodIndex), "  ", methodStrays(methodIndex), "  ", methodFrames(methodIndex), "  "
      Print methodBlitFrames(methodIndex), "  ", methodPasses(methodIndex), "  ", methodPasses(methodIndex)*#CELL_ROWS*#WORLD_WORDS
      If methodBroken(methodIndex) = True Then Print "  BROKEN: stopped, a pass had more than ", #BROKEN_WORDS, " words wrong"
      NPrint ""
    Next
    NPrint "(0 Block; 1 own blit, BLTDPT first; 2 the same with a second wait; 3 own blit, BLTDPT last)"
    NPrint ""
    NPrint "the first ", #KEPT_MAX, " words kept: method  round  bitmap  plane  x  y  found  kind  address"
    For keptIndex.w = 0 To keptCount - 1
      Print keptMethod(keptIndex), "  ", keptPass(keptIndex), "  ", keptBitmap(keptIndex), "  ", keptPlane(keptIndex), "  "
      Print keptX(keptIndex), "  ", keptY(keptIndex), "  $", Right$(Hex$(keptFound(keptIndex) AND $FFFF), 4), "  "
      If keptMissing(keptIndex) = True
        Print "missing"
      Else
        Print "stray"
      EndIf
      NPrint "  $", Hex$(keptAddress(keptIndex))
    Next
    CloseFile 0
    DefaultOutput
  EndIf
End Statement

;; From Blitz mode: to Amiga mode for the file, and back (as the game's EnsureTileSet{} does for its loads).
Statement SaveProgress{}
  QAMIGA
  WriteResults{}
  BLITZ
End Statement

BitMap #WORLD_A_BM, #WORLD_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #WORLD_B_BM, #WORLD_W, #WORLD_H, 4
BitMap #SOURCE_BM, 16, 16, 4
BitMap #HUD_BM, #HUD_W, #HUD_H, 4
BitMap #BACK_BM, #BACK_W, #BACK_H, 4
; Pen 0 dark blue, pen 15 white (the tile), the HUD's pen 1 grey, the back's pens (16 to 31) a dark grey.
InitPalette 0, 32
AGAPalRGB 0, 0, 0, 0, 80
AGAPalRGB 0, 1, 128, 128, 128
AGAPalRGB 0, 15, 255, 255, 255
AGAPalRGB 0, 17, 60, 60, 60

; In Amiga mode still: the bitmaps as allocated (a plane at 0 is an allocation that failed).
stageTrail$ = "bitmaps allocated: bytes a row " + Str$(Peek.w(Addr BitMap(#WORLD_A_BM)))
stageTrail$ = stageTrail$ + ", bitmap 0 plane 0 $" + Hex$(Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#WORLD_A_BM) + 8))
stageTrail$ = stageTrail$ + ", plane 3 $" + Hex$(Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#WORLD_A_BM) + 20))
stageTrail$ = stageTrail$ + ", bitmap 1 plane 0 $" + Hex$(Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#WORLD_B_BM) + 8))
stageTrail$ = stageTrail$ + ", plane 3 $" + Hex$(Peek.l(Addr BitMap(#WORLD_B_BM) + 20)) + Chr$(10)
WriteStages{}

BLITZ

Use BitMap #HUD_BM
Cls 0
Boxf 0, #HUD_H - 2, #HUD_W - 1, #HUD_H - 1, 1
Use BitMap #BACK_BM
Cls 0
For backX.w = 0 To #BACK_W - 64 Step 64
  Boxf backX, 120, backX + 31, 200, 1
Next
InitCopList 0, #HUD_LINE, #HUD_H, #HUD_FLAGS, 0, 32, 0
InitCopList 1, #HUD_LINE + #HUD_H + #LIST_GAP, #VIEW_H, #WORLD_FLAGS, 8, 0, 0
DisplayControls 1, 0, #PF2_OFFSET, 0
DisplayAdjust 0, 0, 0, 0, 31, -33
DisplayAdjust 1, 0, 0, 0, 31, -33
CreateDisplay 0, 1
DisplayPalette 0, 0
DisplayBitMap 0, #HUD_BM, -32, 0
DisplayBitMap 1, #WORLD_A_BM, -32, #VIEW_TOP, #BACK_BM, -32, #VIEW_TOP

MarkStage{"in Blitz mode, the display up"}

Use BitMap #SOURCE_BM
Cls 0
Boxf 0, 0, 15, 15, 15
AutoCookie Off
GetaShape #TILE_SHAPE, 0, 0, 16, 16

MarkStage{"shape cut"}
For methodIndex.w = 0 To #METHODS - 1
  methodMissing(methodIndex) = 0
  methodStrays(methodIndex) = 0
  methodBroken(methodIndex) = False
  methodPasses(methodIndex) = 0
  methodBlitFrames(methodIndex) = 0
  framesBefore.l = CiaFrames{}
  For roundIndex.w = 1 To #ROUNDS
    If methodBroken(methodIndex) = False
      progressColour = methodColour(methodIndex)
      If roundIndex MOD 2 = 0 Then progressColour = (methodColour(methodIndex)/2) AND $777
      wrongBefore.l = methodMissing(methodIndex) + methodStrays(methodIndex)
      Use BitMap #WORLD_A_BM
      Cls 0
      Use BitMap #WORLD_B_BM
      Cls 0
      ; The first round's first pass marks each step (the trail file); the rest do not, to keep the timing clean.
      If roundIndex = 1 Then MarkStage{"method " + Str$(methodIndex) + " round 1: both cleared"}
      For passIndex.w = 1 To #PASSES_A_ROUND
        markThisPass.w = False
        If roundIndex = 1 AND passIndex = 1 Then markThisPass = True
        blitBefore.l = CiaFrames{}
        BlitCheckerboard{#WORLD_A_BM, methodIndex, markThisPass}
        BlitCheckerboard{#WORLD_B_BM, methodIndex, False}
        WaitBlitter
        If markThisPass = False Then methodBlitFrames(methodIndex) = methodBlitFrames(methodIndex) + CiaFrames{} - blitBefore
        methodPasses(methodIndex) = methodPasses(methodIndex) + 1
      Next
      If roundIndex = 1 Then MarkStage{"method " + Str$(methodIndex) + " round 1: all passes blitted"}
      ScanBitmap{#WORLD_A_BM, methodIndex, roundIndex}
      ScanBitmap{#WORLD_B_BM, methodIndex, roundIndex}
      If roundIndex = 1 Then MarkStage{"method " + Str$(methodIndex) + " round 1: both scanned"}
      If methodMissing(methodIndex) + methodStrays(methodIndex) - wrongBefore > #BROKEN_WORDS Then methodBroken(methodIndex) = True
      ; The file after every round, so a run cut short has the strays found so far.
      methodFrames(methodIndex) = CiaFrames{} - framesBefore
      methodsDone = methodIndex + 1
      SaveProgress{}
    EndIf
  Next
Next

AMIGA
End
